From: postmarketOS rhodep port
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: cw2217: do not report FULL while discharging

At 100% with the charger unplugged the gauge reports `Full` rather than
`Discharging`. UPower turns that into `on-battery: no`, PowerDevil keeps
the plugged-in policy, and a locked screen never leads to a suspend. Every
attempt to measure the phone's locked-screen behaviour at 100% therefore
measured nothing at all; the run that finally worked did so only because
the battery had drifted down to 95% first.

The cause is the order of the tests:

	if (cw->soc >= 100)
		return POWER_SUPPLY_STATUS_FULL;
	...
	cur = CW2217_CURRENT_TO_UA(cw->current_raw, cw->shunt_mohm);

The state of charge is checked before the current is looked at, so a pack
at 100% reads FULL whether or not it is being drained. FULL is meant to say
the battery is full *and* not discharging, and it is the only thing
userspace has to decide whether the machine is running on battery.

Read the current first and let a discharge win. Keep FULL for 100% with
nothing leaving, which is the case it is for. Note this driver's sign
convention: positive current is charging.

Below 100% the outcome is unchanged. |cur| under the noise floor is still
NOT_CHARGING, above it the sign still picks CHARGING or DISCHARGING; the
boundary is kept exactly where it was by testing against the negated
threshold rather than abs().

The one case where the state of charge should still decide alone is having
no shunt value, since then no current can be computed at all, so that path
keeps returning FULL at 100% and UNKNOWN otherwise.

--- a/drivers/power/supply/cw2217_battery.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/cw2217_battery.c
@@ -187,18 +187,33 @@
 {
 	int cur;
 
-	if (cw->soc >= 100)
-		return POWER_SUPPLY_STATUS_FULL;
-
+	/*
+	 * With no shunt value there is no current to compute, so the state of
+	 * charge is all there is to go on. This is the only case where it
+	 * decides on its own.
+	 */
 	if (!cw->shunt_mohm)
-		return POWER_SUPPLY_STATUS_UNKNOWN;
+		return cw->soc >= 100 ? POWER_SUPPLY_STATUS_FULL :
+					POWER_SUPPLY_STATUS_UNKNOWN;
 
 	cur = CW2217_CURRENT_TO_UA(cw->current_raw, cw->shunt_mohm);
-	if (abs(cur) < CW2217_CURRENT_NOISE_UA)
-		return POWER_SUPPLY_STATUS_NOT_CHARGING;
 
-	return cur > 0 ? POWER_SUPPLY_STATUS_CHARGING :
-			 POWER_SUPPLY_STATUS_DISCHARGING;
+	/*
+	 * Current leaving the pack means it is discharging, whatever the gauge
+	 * says about the state of charge. This has to be tested before the
+	 * 100% case: a full battery being drained is still being drained, and
+	 * FULL is what userspace reads as "not on battery".
+	 */
+	if (cur <= -CW2217_CURRENT_NOISE_UA)
+		return POWER_SUPPLY_STATUS_DISCHARGING;
+
+	if (cw->soc >= 100)
+		return POWER_SUPPLY_STATUS_FULL;
+
+	if (cur >= CW2217_CURRENT_NOISE_UA)
+		return POWER_SUPPLY_STATUS_CHARGING;
+
+	return POWER_SUPPLY_STATUS_NOT_CHARGING;
 }
 
 static int cw2217_get_health(struct cw2217 *cw)
